course: dictionary
lesson: 14350
title: A word from Ireland
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words are names, and some come from other languages. «The Oireachtas meets in Dublin to make the laws of Ireland.» Oireachtas is the name of Ireland's parliament, so it has a capital letter, and the words around it tell you what it does.
explain: Oireachtas is an Irish (Gaelic) word. It is not an English word, but people in Ireland use it when they speak English. The clues are «make the laws», «meets» and «Dublin», so it must be a place where Ireland's laws are made.
explain: Check by swapping in your meaning: «The parliament of Ireland meets in Dublin to make the laws of Ireland.» It still makes sense, so you have worked it out correctly. If a word is still a mystery, look it up in a dictionary.
fact: The Oireachtas is the national parliament of Ireland.
fact: The Oireachtas is made of the President, the Dáil and the Seanad.
fact: The Dáil is the lower house, and TDs are its members.
fact: The Oireachtas meets in Leinster House in Dublin.
fact: Oireachtas is also the name of a large Irish-language arts festival and an Irish-dancing championship.
exercise: «The Oireachtas makes the laws of Ireland.» What is the Oireachtas? | A shop in Dublin | A type of Irish dance | A river in the west of Ireland | *The national parliament of Ireland
exercise: «The Oireachtas meets in Leinster House.» Where does the Oireachtas meet? | In a school hall in Cork | *In Leinster House in Dublin | At the top of a mountain | In a museum in Galway
exercise: Maya says Oireachtas is an English word. Is she right? | *No, it is an Irish (Gaelic) word that is used in Irish English | Yes, it comes from Latin | Yes, it is a name for a kind of sports team | No, it is a Scottish word for rain
test: «TDs are members of the Dáil.» Which of these is part of the Oireachtas? | The Irish national flag | *The Seanad | The Dublin Zoo | A school in Limerick
test: Who are TDs? | Irish dancers at a championship | Teachers in Dublin | *Members of the Dáil | Members of a football team
exam: «Ciara wants to know which group makes the laws of Ireland.» Which word would answer her question? | The Irish dancing championship | *The Oireachtas | A festival of Irish-language arts | The Dublin Zoo
